---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Release checklist"
   summary="Steps to follow before cutting a public minor or major release. CI handles repeatable checks; this page covers the manual verification that CI cannot."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Pre-release steps</h2>
      <ol>
         <li>Wait for all CI checks to pass.</li>
         <li>Run a manual macOS VoiceOver smoke pass on representative fixtures or demo targets.</li>
         <li>Run a manual Windows NVDA smoke pass on representative fixtures or demo targets.</li>
         <li>Review deferred items and make an explicit accept-or-block decision for each.</li>
         <li>Record what was exercised and any environment constraints that applied.</li>
      </ol>
   </section>

    <section>
       <h2>Required commands</h2>
       <pre><code>npm run standards
npm test
npm run pack:check
a1 help-all
a1 doctor --json</code></pre>
    </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Release record</h2>
      <p>
         The current release record lives in <code>releases/v0.3.0-readiness.md</code>. It documents
         the package release order, the docs publish path, the Agent Skill release path, and deferred
         items.
      </p>
   </section>

    <section>
       <h2>Publish order</h2>
       <ul>
         <li>Packages: publish <code>@a11ied/contracts</code>, <code>@a11ied/wcag-data</code>, <code>@a11ied/wcag-engine</code>, <code>@a11ied/guidepup</code>, <code>@a11ied/core</code>, <code>@a11ied/mcp-server</code>, then <code>a11ied</code> through the <code>publish-packages</code> workflow after <code>npm run standards</code>, <code>npm test</code>, and <code>npm run pack:check</code> pass.</li>
         <li>Docs: build <code>apps/docs/dist/</code> and publish the generated static site.</li>
         <li>Agent Skill: ship <code>skills/a11ied/</code> only after the skill text matches the released CLI and MCP behavior.</li>
       </ul>
   </section>

    <section>
       <h2>Known deferred items</h2>
       <p>
          Some rough edges are tracked and accepted for the current milestone.
          Real-target smoke testing is manual, even though package publication now runs through GitHub Actions.
          See the release record for the full list.
       </p>
    </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Manual smoke tests are required</h2>
      <p>
         VoiceOver and NVDA are the primary target platforms. The virtual reader is useful for
         fast iteration, but releases require confirmation on real assistive technology.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
